gtk: fall back to a surfaceless PlatformDisplay without X11/Wayland

With ENABLE_X11_TARGET=OFF and ENABLE_WAYLAND_TARGET=OFF (QNX: the only EGL is
Screen's, whose EGLNativeDisplayType is an integer handle) createPlatformDisplay()
had no display to return for the GTK port and hit RELEASE_ASSERT_NOT_REACHED, so
every web view (Epiphany at start-up) aborted. Fall back to the surfaceless
display, which the GTK sources already build: the web view then renders without
accelerated compositing when EGL cannot provide it.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/PlatformDisplay.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/PlatformDisplay.cpp
@@ -51,6 +51,10 @@
 #include "PlatformDisplaySurfaceless.h"
 #endif
 
+#if PLATFORM(GTK) && !PLATFORM(WAYLAND) && !PLATFORM(X11) && USE(EGL)
+#include "PlatformDisplaySurfaceless.h"
+#endif
+
 #if PLATFORM(GTK)
 #include "GtkVersioning.h"
 #endif
@@ -161,6 +165,13 @@
     return PlatformDisplayX11::create(nullptr);
 #endif
 
+#if PLATFORM(GTK) && !PLATFORM(WAYLAND) && !PLATFORM(X11) && USE(EGL)
+    // Neither windowing target is built (QNX: its EGL is Screen's and takes no
+    // Display*/wl_display*): a display with no native connection, so the
+    // browser still runs; accelerated compositing is off if EGL refuses it.
+    return PlatformDisplaySurfaceless::create();
+#endif
+
 #if PLATFORM(WPE)
     if (s_useDMABufForRendering) {
 #if USE(GBM)
